# A `var` of a type mutation does not reach yet.
#
# Int and Bool are the whole of what a mutable variable may hold so far.
# A String is a perfectly good Pyking value and a perfectly good `=`
# binding; what it may not be is a cell written to with `:=`.
#
# This program is expected to FAIL type checking. Its `.ast.out` holds
# the error message, not a program's output.

var greeting = "start"
greeting := "hi"
print(greeting)
